MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The magnet wire connects directly to my earlier ferrite cores and electronics supplies because I could use them together to wind coils.",
    "The caliper would help me measure components and mounting clearances across my electronics and mechanical projects, giving it a clear practical use."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The temperature controller and replacement infrared thermometer do not follow from my thermometer purchase: measuring temperature does not establish a need to control it, and I already have a tool for measuring it.",
    "The pressure regulator, vacuum pump and water tester require specific projects that my history does not indicate. Masks and wall anchors also lack a current purpose, while the nut assortment would require knowing the bolt sizes I need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases of tools and project supplies seemed to be taken as interest in almost any workshop equipment, even when it serves a different task.",
    "Shared words or broad purposes seemed to count too much: temperature measurement became temperature control, and an earlier fastener purchase became a reason to suggest unrelated mounting hardware."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Supplies that work with components I already bought matter more to me than equipment that would require starting an unrelated project.",
    "Owning a durable tool reduces my immediate need for another one, and choosing specialized supplies depends on a concrete task and compatible specifications."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my hands-on project interests but stretched them into equipment needs that my purchases do not establish."
}
